<!--
  Hand-written sample of `xcrun xctrace export` with xpath '/trace-toc/run[1]/data/table[@schema="os-signpost"]'
  (xctrace 16.0, Xcode 26.6), in the same style as sample-export: row children are positional in
  <schema> column order, an empty cell is <sentinel/>, repeated values are interned (first
  occurrence id="N", later ones <tag ref="N"/>, inside metadata cells too), a %ld of -1 is
  exported as uint64 18446744073709551615, the emit-location column is elided, and the table is
  split over two <node> elements with only the first carrying <schema>.

  Shape: a capture of the inbound path since the push-conversion (#45, 6.0.0-rc5), where each
  TransportRead and its InboundChunk are emitted back to back on the delivery thread of their own
  connection. Two delivery threads, NIO-SGLTN-1-#1 (0x101) and NIO-SGLTN-1-#2 (0x103), whose
  reads and chunks interleave in time; the ServiceDispatch / ServicePass / RecvDrain rows sit on
  RandomPlayer (0x102). Run with scripts/profile-summary.sh in its default (per-thread) mode.
  no-transport-read-export/os-signpost.xml is this file with every TransportRead row removed.

  Timeline (ns), subsystem ro.SimpleKube.AMSMB2 / category Inbound:
    1. attach carry-over: InboundChunk 1000 @1.000000000 on 0x101 with no read before it
         pass 1: ServiceDispatch 1.000050000-1.000150000 (0.100 ms), ServicePass 1.000160000-1.001160000 (1.000 ms, terminal=0)
                 RecvDrain 1000, RecvDrain -1 (would-block)
    2. interleaved connections: TransportRead 1500 @1.010000000 on 0x101, TransportRead 500 @1.010100000 on 0x103,
                                InboundChunk 500 @1.010200000 on 0x103 (hop 0.100 ms), InboundChunk 1500 @1.010400000 on 0x101 (hop 0.400 ms)
         pass 2: ServiceDispatch 1.010450000-1.010650000 (0.200 ms), ServicePass 1.010660000-1.012660000 (2.000 ms, terminal=0)
                 RecvDrain 2000, RecvDrain -1
    3. byte mismatch: TransportRead 800 @1.020000000 on 0x101 -> InboundChunk 900 @1.020300000 on 0x101 (pairing error)
         pass 3: ServiceDispatch 1.020350000-1.020650000 (0.300 ms), ServicePass 1.020660000-1.022160000 (1.500 ms, terminal=0)
                 RecvDrain 900, RecvDrain -1
    4. superseded read: TransportRead 600 @1.030000000 on 0x103, TransportRead 700 @1.030200000 on 0x103 (the 600 read never
                        gets a chunk), InboundChunk 700 @1.030500000 on 0x103 (hop 0.300 ms, pairs with the 700 read)
         pass 4: ServiceDispatch 1.030550000-1.030950000 (0.400 ms), ServicePass 1.030960000-1.035300000 (4.340 ms, terminal=1)
                 RecvDrain 700, RecvDrain 0 (EOF)
    idle gap of 1.965 s (> 1 s, excluded from the active window), then
    5. trailing read: TransportRead 400 @3.000000000 on 0x101 with no chunk before the end of the capture

  Expected numbers in per-thread mode (nearest-rank percentiles, 1-based index ceil(N*p/100)):
    TransportRead  n=6  bytes 4500  sorted [400,500,600,700,800,1500] -> min 400, median idx3=600, p95 idx6=1500, max 1500
    InboundChunk   n=5  bytes 4600  sorted [500,700,900,1000,1500]    -> 500 / idx3=900 / idx5=1500 / 1500
    RecvDrain      n=8  bytes 4600  copied 4, EOF 1, would-block 3; sizes [700,900,1000,2000] -> 700 / idx2=900 / idx4=2000 / 2000
    ServiceDispatch n=4 [0.100,0.200,0.300,0.400] ms -> 0.100 / idx2=0.200 / idx4=0.400 / 0.400
    ServicePass    n=4, non-terminal 3 [1.000,1.500,2.000] -> 1.000 / idx2=1.500 / idx3=2.000 / 2.000; terminal 1 listed: 4.340
    ratio 6/5 = 1.20; 2 delivery threads (0x101, 0x103); zero-byte skipped 0
    per thread 0x101: chunk 1000 without a read; read 1500 -> chunk 1500 paired (0.400 ms); read 800 -> chunk 900 mismatch
                      (consumes both); read 400 still pending at the end -> read without a chunk
    per thread 0x103: read 500 -> chunk 500 paired (0.100 ms); read 600 superseded by read 700 -> read without a chunk;
                      read 700 -> chunk 700 paired (0.300 ms)
    pump-hop [0.100,0.300,0.400] -> 0.100 / idx2=0.300 / idx3=0.400 / 0.400; 3 pairs, 1 chunk without a read,
             2 reads without a chunk, 1 pairing error  (3+1+1 = 5 chunks; 3+2+1+0 = 6 reads)
    buffered 4600-4600 = 0
    span 3.000000-1.000000 = 2.000000 s -> 4600/2.0 = 2300 B/s = 0.002 MB/s
    active = 1.035300-1.000000 = 0.035300 s -> 4600/0.0353 = 130312 B/s = 0.130 MB/s

  What the global byte-sum FIFO (the pre-#45 pairing, selected with the pairing option set to global) reports for the same rows,
  which is the defect per-thread pairing fixes: the carry-over chunk finds an empty FIFO
  (underflow, 0 bytes queued); in group 2 the 500 chunk pops the 1500 read (overshoot, 1 read
  sums to 1500) and the 1500 chunk then finds only the 500 read (underflow); the 900 chunk finds
  only 800 bytes (underflow); the 700 chunk pops 600 then 700 (overshoot, 2 reads sum to 1300).
  Result: 0 pairs, 5 pairing errors, reads per chunk: none, pump-hop latency n/a, and the 400
  read is left in the FIFO unreported.
